# Translation script for set.mm. Syntax, axioms, and variables are
# translated automatically, so the script only says how far to go and lists
# fixups (skip LABEL, assume LABEL, replace LABEL followed by copied lines
# ending with --, prove LABEL followed by a Ghilbert proof body ending with
# --, prove_instance LABEL with the same kind of body, bound_form LABEL...).
# Fixups must appear in set.mm order.
#
# This currently covers propositional and predicate calculus, stopping
# before ZF set theory at the `stop` command. The option --all of mm_xlat
# ignores it, and translates all of set.mm.

# When a proof step makes two setvars that bind the same variable, the
# translator writes an instance of the statement it uses, named like ax-11.y=x,
# and replays the statement's proof with them identified. Axioms have no such
# proof, so their instances are proved by hand.
prove_instance ax-11.y=x
  l0: id;
--
prove_instance ax-12.y=x
  l0: ala1;
  l1: a1i _;
--
prove_instance ax-c11.y=x
  l0: id;
  l1: a1i _;
--

# The theorems proved by hand below have set.mm proofs that need two setvars
# that bind to be the same variable at some step, which Ghilbert doesn't
# allow (bound variables are always distinct). The statement is still
# generated from set.mm; only the proof is replaced.
